 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Sales order {{v2}} is cancelled and no longer active. Clicking {{v1}} on the confirmed sales order opened Odoo's \"{{v1}} Sales Order\" wizard (\"Are you sure you want to cancel this order?\"); its buttons ignored mouse clicks, so I submitted the wizard's primary action with the keyboard instead. Odoo then displayed the status \"Cancelled\": in the statusbar the radio \"Cancelled\" is checked and disabled, all other states (Sales Order, Quotation Sent, Quotation) are greyed out, the Confirm/Send/Invoice buttons are gone and only Preview and Set to Quotation remain. I verified this survived a full page reload of record id={{v4}}, so it is persisted. A \"Delivery failure\" notification appeared in the chatter because the wizard tried to email the customer and this environment has no mail server — that is a side effect, not a failure of the cancellation.",
